'''''Melianthus major''''', the '''giant honey flower''' or '''{{Lang|af|kruidjie-roer-my-nie}}''' ([[Afrikaans]] for 'herb-touch-me-not'), is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Francoaceae]]. It is an [[evergreen]] suckering [[shrub]], [[endemism|endemic]] to South Africa and naturalised in India, Australia and New Zealand.<ref name="plantzafrica">{{cite web |title=''Melianthus major'' |url=https://pza.sanbi.org/melianthus-major |accessdate=2023-02-26 |work=PlantZAfrica.com |publisher=South African National Biodiversity Institute}}</ref><ref name=Blood>{{cite book|author=Blood, Kate.| title=Environmental weeds: a field guide for SE Australia|publisher=Bloomings Books|location=Melbourne, Australia | year=2001 | isbn=0957908601}}</ref> It grows to {{convert|2|-|3|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|1|-|3|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} wide, with [[pinnate]] blue-green leaves {{convert|30|-|50|cm|0|abbr=on}} long, which have a distinctive musky odour. Dark red, nectar-laden flower spikes, {{convert|30|-|80|cm|0|abbr=on}} in length, appear in spring, followed by green pods.<ref name=plantzafrica/><ref name=RHSAZ>{{cite book|title=RHS A-Z encyclopedia of garden plants|year=2008|publisher=Dorling Kindersley|location=United Kingdom|isbn=978-1405332965|pages=1136}}</ref> All parts of the plants are poisonous.<ref name = Blood/>

The Latin [[Binomial nomenclature|binomial]] ''Melianthus major'' literally means "large honey flower".<ref name=AZPLA>{{cite book|last=Coombes|first=Allen J.|title=The A to Z of plant names|year=2012|publisher=Timber Press|location=USA|isbn=9781604691962|pages=[https://archive.org/details/isbn_9781604691962/page/312 312]|url-access=registration|url=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9781604691962/page/312}}</ref> The plant is also sometimes called ''honeybush'' ([[List of plants known as honeybush|along with many other plants]])''.''

In cultivation this plant requires a sheltered location and may also need a protective winter [[mulch]] in [[temperateness|temperate]] regions. It has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web|title=RHS Plant Selector - ''Melianthus major''|url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/84304/Melianthus-major/Details | access-date = 3 January 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web  | url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf | title = AGM Plants - Ornamental | date = July 2017 | page = 64 
| publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | accessdate = 4 April 2018}}</ref> 

